From 8fa825374374e48ea7a1bc8bf687a7e25d5476b5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: William Emerison Six <billsix@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 03:25:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 376/488] soh: name the 34 address-named symbols defined in
 z_en_poh.c

SoH carries the Ocarina of Time decomp, in which several thousand symbols are
still named after their ROM address. This commit names every such symbol DEFINED
IN ONE FILE, so the work can be reviewed a file at a time.

The file names the unit; it does not bound it. Each rename is applied wherever
the symbol occurs -- the declaration in the header, the definition, and every
call site -- so this commit reaches into whatever other files use these symbols
and leaves no dangling reference. It is a pure rename: no behaviour changes, and
the only edits that are not renames are the provenance comments described below.

Two name sources are used, and every name says which it came from:

  * zeldaret/oot -- SoH's decomp IS zeldaret/oot at the same ROM addresses, so
    where oot has already named a symbol, that name is adopted verbatim. The
    definition gets a "Name from zeldaret/oot" comment and every declaration a
    short "// was <addr> [oot]" tag.

  * DEDUCED -- oot leaves a great many symbols address-named too, so those
    names are inferred from the body and its callers, and are marked as OURS
    rather than passed off as upstream. The definition gets
    "LLM generated name (HIGH|GUESS), was <addr>: <reason>" and the short tag
    reads "[LLM:HIGH]" or "[LLM:GUESS]". A GUESS is tagged at every call site
    as well, not only the declaration, so a reader who meets the name anywhere
    knows it is inferred. "git grep '[LLM:'" lists every place the decomp
    leans on an inference.

The justification recorded for each individual name follows, one entry per
symbol, in the order the renames were made. Nothing is summarised away: these
are the per-commit reasons from the unsquashed history, with the boilerplate
that was identical in every one of them hoisted into the text above.

All 34 are defined in soh/src/overlays/actors/ovl_En_Poh/z_en_poh.c.

  * func_80ADE114 -> EnPoh_SetupHover
    deduced, confidence HIGH: loops the first idle animation, arms a short
    timer and stops the poe in place

  * func_80ADE1BC -> EnPoh_SetupApproach
    deduced, confidence HIGH: loops the second idle animation and starts
    drifting at speed 2

  * func_80ADE28C -> EnPoh_SetupDamage
    deduced, confidence HIGH: plays the damaged animation, aims the
    knockback away from the attacker and applies the red color filter

  * func_80ADE368 -> EnPoh_SetupFlee
    deduced, confidence HIGH: morphs to the flee animation, turns away from
    the player and arms the 200-frame retreat

  * func_80ADE48C -> EnPoh_SetupDissolve
    deduced, confidence HIGH: stops the poe, drops targeting and starts the
    death dissolve

  * func_80ADE4C8 -> EnPoh_SetupSpinAway
    deduced, confidence HIGH: plays the idle animation once while backing
    off at -5 speed

  * func_80ADE514 -> EnPoh_SetupTurnAround
    deduced, confidence HIGH: records the opposite heading and stops while
    the poe turns onto it

  * func_80ADE6D4 -> EnPoh_SetupSoulRise
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the soul flame's start: zeroes the light and
    scale, picks its color from the poe type and plays the appear sound

  * func_80ADE950 -> EnPoh_SetupSoulVanish
    deduced, confidence HIGH: installs the fade-out action, optionally
    laughing as the flame goes

  * func_80ADE998 -> EnPoh_SetupTalkRegular
    deduced, confidence HIGH: installs the ordinary poe soul's conversation
    action

  * func_80ADE9BC -> EnPoh_SetupTalkComposer
    deduced, confidence HIGH: installs the composer brothers' conversation
    action

  * func_80ADEA5C -> EnPoh_TurnTowardHome
    deduced, confidence HIGH: re-aims the drift heading at the home position
    once the poe strays past 400 units, and steps the yaw onto it

  * func_80ADEAC4 -> EnPoh_Hover
    deduced, confidence HIGH: hovers at the player's height until the player
    comes within 200 units or the timer runs out

  * func_80ADEC9C -> EnPoh_Approach
    deduced, confidence HIGH: closes on the player, turning to face them and
    speeding up for the strike

  * func_80ADEECC -> EnPoh_Damage
    deduced, confidence HIGH: rides the knockback out, then flees or
    dissolves according to remaining health

  * func_80ADEF38 -> EnPoh_RegularAppear
    deduced, confidence HIGH: fades the ordinary poe in over its appear
    animation, the counterpart of EnPoh_ComposerAppear

  * func_80ADF15C -> EnPoh_Dissolve
    deduced, confidence HIGH: rings EffectSsDeadDb outward as the body
    breaks up, ending with NA_SE_EN_PO_DEAD2

  * func_80ADF574 -> EnPoh_SpinAway
    deduced, confidence HIGH: spins the poe as it drifts backwards, then
    returns to the idle

  * func_80ADF5E0 -> EnPoh_TurnAround
    deduced, confidence HIGH: turns onto the recorded heading, breaking off
    early if the player comes close

  * func_80ADF894 -> EnPoh_Flee
    deduced, confidence HIGH: weaves away from the player at a sine offset
    until the retreat timer expires or the player falls behind

  * func_80ADFA90 -> EnPoh_StepAlpha
    deduced, confidence HIGH: steps the soul flame's alpha by the caller's
    amount and rescales, repositions and relights it to match

  * func_80ADFE28 -> EnPoh_SoulRise
    deduced, confidence HIGH: floats the flame upward while fading it in,
    then opens the conversation

  * func_80ADFE80 -> EnPoh_SoulWaitForTalk
    deduced, confidence HIGH: bobs the flame and offers the conversation
    while the player touches it, fading out when the timer expires

  * func_80AE009C -> EnPoh_SoulVanish
    deduced, confidence HIGH: fades the flame out at 13 alpha a frame and
    kills the actor

  * func_80AE032C -> EnPoh_UpdateDamage
    deduced, confidence HIGH: applies an AC hit, playing the death or damage
    cry and entering the damage state

  * func_80AE067C -> EnPoh_UpdateLightColor
    deduced, confidence HIGH: drives the lantern colour from the current
    action: red while attacking, green-blue while fleeing, flashing while
    damaged

  * func_80AE089C -> EnPoh_UpdateEnvColor
    deduced, confidence HIGH: ramps the body's env colour in during the
    appear animations and flickers it randomly afterwards

  * D_80AE1A50 -> sRupeePoeCount
    deduced, confidence HIGH: counts the live EN_POH_RUPEE poes; the third
    and later ones kill themselves instead of dropping a rupee

  * D_80AE1B4C -> sSharpEnvColor
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the env colour EnPoh_DrawComposer uses for
    Sharp

  * D_80AE1B50 -> sFlatEnvColor
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the env colour EnPoh_DrawComposer uses for
    Flat

  * D_80AE1B54 -> sSharpAccentColor
    deduced, confidence HIGH: Sharp's second colour, bound to the other
    segment in the same draw

  * D_80AE1B58 -> sFlatAccentColor
    deduced, confidence HIGH: Flat's second colour, bound to the other
    segment in the same draw

  * D_80AE1B60 -> sDeadDbVelocity
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the upward velocity handed to every
    EffectSsDeadDb of the dissolve

  * D_80AE1B6C -> sDeadDbAccel
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the zero acceleration handed to those same
    effects

